## No node name here. The Burrito-packaged binary boots the BEAM directly from
## this file for every subcommand, and a fixed `-name` would make a one-off
## command such as `symphony check` clash with a running Symphony before any
## Elixir code runs. The service starts distribution itself as
## symphony@127.0.0.1 (SymphonyElixir.ReleaseNode); the bin/symphony script gets
## the same name from env.sh. Mnesia disc_copies are tagged with node(), so the
## service's stable node name is what reopens the on-disk RunStore schema.
##
## The cookie is a secret and is NOT set here: the script launcher reads it via
## env.sh, the Burrito launcher via SymphonyElixir.ReleaseCookie.

## Distribution exists only for local remote-console / observer access (the
## control plane is HTTP), so bind the distribution listener to loopback.
-kernel inet_dist_use_interface {127,0,0,1}
